//
// Per sample: the peak of the incoming audio is estimated at 4x oversampling (a windowed-sinc polyphase interpolator)
// and turned into the gain that keeps it under the ceiling. A sliding minimum over the lookahead window holds that
// gain, a one-pole release lets it recover, and a moving average over the same window smooths the attack into a ramp.
// The audio is delayed by the window, so the gain is fully down before a peak arrives: no overshoot, no clipping and
// no hard gain steps (a hard step is what distorts). Stereo linked: one gain for every channel.
//
// The file is plain JavaScript with no imports so the worklet can load it on its own (Vite ships it as an asset with
// \`?url\`). The core class is exported for the unit tests; the processor registers only inside an AudioWorklet.

const DEFAULTS = { lookaheadMs: 5, ceilingDb: -1.2, releaseMs: 110, oversample: 4, tapsPerPhase: 24 };

